<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Soccer-Ireland's Given out of Wales game.</title>
<headline>Soccer-Ireland's Given out of Wales game.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Blackburn Rovers goalkeeper Shay Given on Monday withdrew from the 20-man Republic of Ireland squad for the friendly international against Wales in Cardiff on February 11.</p>
<p>Given, 21, is having treatment for a stomach strain.</p>
<p>His withdrawal could leave the way open for Keith Branagan, of Bolton Wanderers, to make his senior debut.</p>
<p>--Damien Lynch, Dublin newsroom 353-1-661-3377.</p>
